<h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
<p>
  The <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/">Ruby on Rails</a> web framework
  provides a library called
  <a href="https://guides.rubyonrails.org/active_record_querying.html">ActiveRecord</a>,
  and a database-backed cache store called
  <a href="https://guides.rubyonrails.org/caching_with_rails.html#solid-cache">Solid Cache</a>.
</p>
<p>
  This page lists call patterns that interpolate unbound input into SQL run
  against the same database connection Solid Cache uses for
  <code>solid_cache_entries</code>. Careless use of these patterns lets SQL
  injection reach the cache table itself, not just application tables.
</p>
<p>
  Please use this list as a guide of what <em>not</em> to do.
</p>
<h3>Examples</h3>
<p>
  Each entry below shows the query run, the SQL it produced, and the
  resulting row(s) - including, where relevant, the
  <code>solid_cache_entries</code> rows it wrote. The examples on this page
  were tested with <b>Rails 8.0.5</b> and Postgres.
</p>
<h3>Interactive Version</h3>
<p>
  Clone and run this site from
  <a href="https://github.com/presidentbeef/inject-some-sql">the git repo</a>
  to try out or modify the examples!
</p>
